---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../utils/schema';
import { COUNTRIES } from '../../data/countries';
import { SITE, abs } from '../../site';

const breadcrumb = breadcrumbSchema([
  { name: SITE.name, url: abs('/') },
  { name: 'About', url: abs('/about/') },
]);
---

<Base
  title={`About ${SITE.name}`}
  description={`${SITE.name} is a free invoice generator that knows the tax and invoicing rules of ${COUNTRIES.length} countries. No sign-up, no watermark, and your data never leaves your browser.`}
  schema={breadcrumb}
>
  <article class="about-wrap" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">{SITE.name}</a><span aria-hidden="true">›</span><span aria-current="page">About</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="about-header">
        <h1 id="about-heading" class="about-heading">About {SITE.name}</h1>
        <p class="about-lead">{SITE.tagline}. Free, private, and honest about what a PDF invoice can and can’t do.</p>
      </header>

      <section class="about-section">
        <h2>Why it exists</h2>
        <p>
          Most free invoice generators are the same form with a “Tax %” box. That’s fine until you need
          CGST + SGST in India, HST that depends on the Canadian province, IRPF withheld in Spain, the
          §19 note in Germany or VAT plus two levies in Ghana. Then you’re left guessing.
        </p>
        <p>
          {SITE.name} covers {COUNTRIES.length} countries. Pick yours and the invoice sets itself up correctly,
          down to the payment methods people there actually use, whether that’s a SEPA transfer, UPI or mobile money.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section">
        <h2>What makes it different</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Country tax presets, including multiple tax lines, tax-inclusive pricing and withholding</li>
          <li>Each country page lists the legally required invoice details, with sources and the date they were last checked</li>
          <li>Any currency, 7 invoice languages, A4 or US Letter</li>
          <li>Payment QR codes: SEPA for euro IBANs, UPI for India, or any payment link</li>
          <li>Invoices, quotes, receipts, proformas and credit notes</li>
          <li>No account and no upload; free invoices carry only a small “Made with” line</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section">
        <h2>How it works</h2>
        <p>
          Everything runs in your browser. There is no server-side database and no login: your business
          details, saved clients and invoice history are kept in your browser’s local storage, and PDFs are
          generated on your device. Use <strong>Export backup</strong> to move them to another device.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section">
        <h2>Keeping the data right</h2>
        <p>
          Rates and rules come from tax authorities and reputable tax summaries, and each country shows
          when it was last checked. Rules change, and people doing business in a country often notice
          first. If something is wrong, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and we’ll fix it.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-wrap { padding: 3rem 0 5rem; }
  .about-heading { font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem); line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -0.025em; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .about-lead { font-size: 1.0625rem; color: var(--text-3); line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 0; }
  .about-section { margin-top: 2.5rem; padding-top: 2.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .about-section h2 { font-size: 1.125rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text); letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .about-section p { font-size: 0.9375rem; color: var(--text-2); line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .about-section p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .about-section ul { margin: 0.5rem 0 0 1.25rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; }
  .about-section li { font-size: 0.9375rem; color: var(--text-2); line-height: 1.65; }
  .about-section a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .about-section a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
